<!-- VARFÖR DET FUNGERAR -->
<section class="section alt" id="varfor">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why our approach works</p>
      <h2>Our methodology is not built on assumptions.</h2>
      <p class="section-desc">It is built on how modern B2B buyers actually make decisions. Research from Gartner, Forrester and McKinsey shows that:</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card-grid two">
      <div class="card research-card reveal">
        <p class="research-claim">Enterprise deals involve on average <strong>10–13 decision-makers</strong> and stakeholders.</p>
        <p class="research-sources">Sources:
          <a href="https://www.forrester.com/press-newsroom/forrester-the-state-of-business-buying-2024/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Forrester</a>
          <a href="https://www.geisheker.com/how-b2b-companies-make-buying-decisions/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Geisheker</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card research-card reveal">
        <p class="research-claim">Buyers spend only <strong>a small part of their buying journey</strong> in direct contact with suppliers.</p>
        <p class="research-sources">Sources:
          <a href="https://www.gartner.com/en/sales/insights/b2b-buying-journey" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gartner</a>
          <a href="https://growthmethod.com/gartner-b2b-buying-journey/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Growth Method</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card research-card reveal">
        <p class="research-claim"><strong>86%</strong> of B2B purchases stall or are delayed during the buying process.</p>
        <p class="research-sources">Sources:
          <a href="https://www.forrester.com/press-newsroom/forrester-the-state-of-business-buying-2024/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Forrester</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card research-card reveal">
        <p class="research-claim">Leading growth companies increasingly work <strong>account-based</strong>, focusing on personalisation, prioritisation and buyer alignment.</p>
        <p class="research-sources">Sources:
          <a href="https://www.mckinsey.com/capabilities/growth-marketing-and-sales/our-insights/the-surprising-economics-of-b2b-growth-the-new-survival-threshold-and-what-it-takes-to-thrive" target="_blank" rel="noopener">McKinsey (1)</a>
          <a href="https://www.mckinsey.com/capabilities/growth-marketing-and-sales/our-insights/five-fundamental-truths-how-b2b-winners-keep-growing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">McKinsey (2)</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lead-text research-close reveal">
      <p>That is why we don't start with more activity. We start with prioritisation.</p>
      <p><strong>The right market, segment, account and buyer. Only then the deal.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- METODIK -->
<section class="section" id="metodik">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Methodology</p>
      <h2>From market to deal. One level at a time.</h2>
      <p class="section-desc">We don't analyse everything at once. At each level we pick the most promising option and go deeper from there.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card-grid five">
      <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="card-badge">01 · Market</span>
        <h3>Where should you win first?</h3>
        <p class="card-desc">Size, growth, purchasing power, digital maturity and strategic fit.</p>
        <p class="card-outcome"><strong>Outcome:</strong> Prioritised markets.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="card-badge">02 · Segment</span>
        <h3>Where is the need greatest?</h3>
        <p class="card-desc">Problem intensity, purchasing power, competition and strategic relevance.</p>
        <p class="card-outcome"><strong>Outcome:</strong> Prioritised segments.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="card-badge">03 · Account</span>
        <h3>Which companies are worth winning?</h3>
        <p class="card-desc">Problem fit, reference value, scalability and buying signals.</p>
        <p class="card-outcome"><strong>Outcome:</strong> Prioritised target accounts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="card-badge">04 · Buyer</span>
        <h3>How do they buy?</h3>
        <p class="card-desc">Problem owner, budget owner, decision-makers, procurement and blockers.</p>
        <p class="card-outcome"><strong>Outcome:</strong> A map of how the deal must be navigated.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="card-badge">05 · Deal</span>
        <h3>How do we win the deal?</h3>
        <p class="card-desc">Who, which message, why now and the next step, through legal and requirements to a decision.</p>
        <p class="card-outcome"><strong>Outcome:</strong> Deals that reach a decision and a signed contract.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="loop-block reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Lean and agile</p>
      <h3>Deep on the most promising. Then the next.</h3>
      <p class="section-desc">We take the highest-priority opportunity all the way down to a deal. When that branch is done, or shows no potential, we step back one level and move on to the next.</p>
      <ul class="loop-list">
        <li><span>The account shows no potential</span><i>→</i><strong>next account</strong></li>
        <li><span>The segment shows no potential</span><i>→</i><strong>next segment</strong></li>
        <li><span>The market shows no potential</span><i>→</i><strong>next market</strong></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="section-desc">Every customer conversation brings new information. We update priorities and messaging continuously. The market is our feedback loop.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="fit-block reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Before we go one level deeper</p>
      <h3 class="fit-formula">Market Fit <span>×</span> Access Fit <span>×</span> Win Fit</h3>
      <div class="metrics-grid three">
        <div class="metric">
          <span class="metric-label">Market Fit</span>
          <span class="metric-desc">Do enough organisations have the problem?</span>
        </div>
        <div class="metric">
          <span class="metric-label">Access Fit</span>
          <span class="metric-desc">Can we reach the right buyers and influence the process?</span>
        </div>
        <div class="metric">
          <span class="metric-label">Win Fit</span>
          <span class="metric-desc">Do we have a realistic chance of winning the deal?</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="section-desc">If one factor is zero, we move on to the next opportunity.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

